# Confirm when the ask is ambiguous across journal options

If the latest message can mean **more than one named scheme** in
`journals/` or the CLI (option 1 vs 2, strat vs fixedstim, Harris vs
shuffle, split vs unsplit, true / act / bayes prior, **80 vs 150 ms
I/M prior window**, …), **stop and ask** before implementing or
submitting jobs. Do not pick the reading that is easiest to wire or
that matches an older keep-list.

## This repo (incident 2026-08-22)

“Within each shuffle stratum” + fitted AK + copy-last was implemented
as **option 2 (`fixedstim`)** — real stim, labels at real `elig_idx`.
The user meant **option 1 (`strat`)** — new pseudo-session, remake
stim×act-prior (choice) or stim×choice (act_block) on that draw.
A full BWM FDR was run on the wrong arm.

Journal source of truth: [structured_nulls_choice_lr.md](journals/structured_nulls_choice_lr.md)
(option 1 = `_pseudo_strat`, option 2 = `_pseudo_fixed`).

## What to do

1. Name the candidate options in the user’s words (e.g. “option 1
   stratified pseudo” vs “option 2 fixed real stim”).
2. Ask which one. Do not submit ORCD / write the arm until they pick.
3. After they pick, implement **only** that one.

Do not treat “same stratum as shuffle” as approval for `fixedstim`.
Option 1 remakes that stratum **on the pseudo**.

## This repo (incident 2026-09-09)

`gm0` / `mleak` were meant to fix **stim-aligned M after the S peak**
(notch 60–70 ms, climb after 80). They were fit with
`prior_window_ms` unset (legacy **80 ms**) because test 6 said “keep
production window unset” after `im150` lost on *production eval tot*.
That keep-list is about ranking vs regular on 80 ms, not about an
M-shape campaign whose target is invisible to an 80 ms prior term.

**80 vs 150 is a named fork.** If the aim mentions the M/I curve
through 60–150 ms, a post-80 climb, or “the 150 window,” **ask**
before leaving the window unset. Do not inherit “production unset”
from tests 1–6. Before any Stage B submit / add-to-main, state in
one line: **window, stratum, freeze, what the prior SSE can see.**
Do not rank a campaign on a metric the fit never optimized.
